{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnOmegaOrder","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.HahnOmegaOrder","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.RingTheory.HahnSeries.Multiplication","lean:module:QOU.AppendixSurreals.Asymptotics"],"declarations":2,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.hahnOmegaOrder","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.hahnOmegaOrder","kind":"def","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HahnOmegaOrder.lean#L82-L112","doc":"**Hahn series model for `OmegaOrder`.**\n\n`Ow` is the leading exponent `orderTop`, with `⊤` at zero. The four axioms:\n\n* `Ow_zero` — `orderTop 0 = ⊤` by definition;\n* `Ow_mul` — `orderTop_mul` above;\n* `Ow_algebraMap_mul` — a scalar with non-zero image is a constant series, whose\n  `orderTop` is `0`, so multiplying by it shifts the leading exponent by `0`.\n  This is the axiom that was previously phrased with `SurrealField.ofReal`; over\n  a general algebra it is `algebraMap`, and the two agree on any `SurrealField`\n  instantiated at the reals.\n\nDeliberately **not** a global `instance`: it is a witness that the axioms are\nconsistent, and registering it would let typeclass resolution silently pick the\nHahn valuation for an unrelated `K`. Callers name it. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.AppendixSurreals.orderTop_mul","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.AppendixSurreals.orderTop_mul","kind":"theorem","line":63,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/lean/QOU/AppendixSurreals/HahnOmegaOrder.lean#L63-L78","doc":"**`orderTop` is multiplicative over a domain.**\n\nMathlib proves only `orderTop_add_le_mul`, the inequality. The equality that\n`OmegaOrder.Ow_mul` states follows from `HahnSeries.order_mul` on the non-zero\npart, plus the two zero cases — and those need `R` to be a domain a second time,\nso that `x * y = 0` forces `x = 0 ∨ y = 0` and the `⊤` bookkeeping matches. ","signatureChunk":0}]}